2026-10-29T07:25:46.4338551Z == speed, same program, same machine, plain build and --release
2026-10-29T07:25:46.4423225Z   bump pointer      31 ns per allocation, 13 ns --release
2026-10-29T07:25:46.4423680Z   size-class arena  53 ns per allocation, 13 ns --release
2026-10-29T07:25:46.4424207Z   size-class arena  81 ns per alloc+free pair, 7 ns --release
2026-10-29T07:25:46.4425224Z   A size-class allocator is expected to cost more than a bump pointer on
2026-10-29T07:25:46.4425955Z   the fast path. The number is reported rather than hidden, and it is the
2026-10-29T07:25:46.4426273Z   price of a heap that can hand memory back.
2026-10-29T07:25:47.8290366Z   best of 3: bump 13 ns, arena 13 ns, pair 7 ns
